TITLE:: PltMeter
summary:: Peak and RMS level meter, one bar per channel
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltSpectrum, Classes/SendPeakRMS

DESCRIPTION::
A vertical bar per channel: RMS filled, peak as a line, the peak held for a moment
above it, and a red mark at the top when a channel has hit full scale.

Analysis runs on the server with link::Classes/SendPeakRMS:: at the tail of the root
node, so code::In.ar:: sees what everything else has written, and arrives as OSC.

code::pushFrame:: does the same job from the language, so the view can be driven
from any other source, and can be tested without a server.

note::
code::SendPeakRMS:: applies its own decay to the peak, and its default is 3 seconds,
which makes the peak line fall slowly and duplicates the hold line. PltMeter sets
strong::peakLag:: to 0.1 instead and lets strong::holdTime:: do the holding.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: numChannels
argument:: bus
Bus index to read from. 0 is the first output channel.
argument:: server
Defaults to code::Server.default::. Analysis starts at once if it is running,
otherwise call strong::start:: later.
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: start
Create the analysis synth and the responder. A no-op if already running.

METHOD:: stop
Free them. strong::close:: does this too.

METHOD:: pushFrame
One frame of levels, as linear amplitudes.
argument:: argPeaks
argument:: argRms

METHOD:: clipping
True while any channel has hit full scale within the hold time.

METHOD:: peaks
METHOD:: rmss
METHOD:: holds
Current values, as linear amplitudes.

METHOD:: floorDb
Bottom of the scale.
METHOD:: holdTime
Seconds a peak is held.
METHOD:: replyRate
Frames per second from the server.
METHOD:: peakLag
See the note above.
METHOD:: rmsColor
METHOD:: peakColor
METHOD:: clipColor
METHOD:: numChannels
METHOD:: bus
METHOD:: server

EXAMPLES::
code::
s.boot;
m = PltMeter(2, 0).front;             // the first two output channels
x = { PinkNoise.ar(0.3) ! 2 }.play;
x.free;
m.close;

// a wider meter, more headroom shown
m = PltMeter(8, 0, s, "eight channels", 560, 340).floorDb_(-72).front;

// driven from the language
m = PltMeter(4, 0, nil, "from anywhere").front;
m.pushFrame([1.0, 0.5, 0.12, 0.01], [0.7, 0.35, 0.08, 0.004]);
m.clipping;                           // true
::
